      { id: "a10", kick: "DATA", sev: "", time: "15:27", read: 10, author: "Lena Vogt", role: "Threat Intel Lead", date: "JUL 13, 2026", img: "chart: q2 losses by category", rel: ["s3", "s1"],
        title: "Q2 2026 Scam Losses Hit $2.1B — Down 8%, but Drainer Kits Doubled",
        dek: "The quarterly damage report: fewer mega-ponzis, far more industrialized wallet-draining. Where the money actually went, in six charts.",
        body: [
          { k: "p", t: "Total tracked losses fell for a second straight quarter — and yet the median victim lost more. The mix is shifting from slow, social ponzis to instant, technical drains: kit-based wallet drainers took $412M in Q2, more than double a year ago." },
          { k: "h", t: "Where the money went" },
